==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|-}} and {{inh|de|goh|līm}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*līmaz}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*sley-||smooth; slick; sticky; slimy}} (modern {{cog|en|slime}}). Cognate with {{cog|en|lime}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/laɪ̯m/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Leim.ogg|Audio}}
* {{audio|de|De-Leim2.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|aɪ̯m|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m,(e)s}}

# [[glue]]

====Usage notes====
* ''Leim'' is generally restricted to glue used on hard materials, particularly wood. The more general word is {{m|de|Klebstoff}}.

====Declension====
{{de-ndecl|m,(e)s}}

